<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Default (English) strings.

  This file is the fallback for every locale the app does not translate, so an
  unknown system language still produces readable UI rather than raw resource
  names. Chinese lives in values-zh/strings.xml and is a full translation, not a
  partial one: a half-translated screen mixing scripts reads worse than either
  language alone.

  Everything user-visible lives here. Before this, all of it was Chinese string
  literals inside Kotlin, which meant the app could not follow the system
  language at all.
-->
